1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   You may view, read, clone and study this repository for the purpose of
   evaluating the work, reviewing its engineering, or considering a commercial
   arrangement with the copyright holder. You may quote short excerpts in a
   review, an article or an internal assessment, with attribution.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   Without prior written permission from the copyright holder, you may not:

   a. use this software, in whole or in part, in any product, service,
      prototype, pipeline or internal tool, whether commercial or not;
   b. copy, adapt, translate or incorporate any part of it into other work,
      including as training data for a machine learning model;
   c. redistribute, sublicense, publish or sell it, in original or modified
      form;
   d. reuse the prompts, prompt fragments, directive strings, calibrated
      thresholds and measured constants AUTHORED BY THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER and
      contained here, which are the substance of the work rather than
      incidental to it. This clause claims nothing over third-party material
      recorded in the knowledge base — see section 5.


3. THIRD-PARTY STATEMENTS RECORDED IN THE KNOWLEDGE BASE

   The knowledge base under `studio/knowledge/` records what other people
   published about generation models: vendor documentation, papers, and
   statements practitioners posted in public discussions on HuggingFace and
   Civitai. Each record carries the URL it came from and the date the source
   stated it.

   Those statements are their authors' work, not the copyright holder's.
   Clause 2(d) does not claim them, and this licence grants no rights over
   them. They are quoted, in short and with attribution to the source page,
   for the purpose named at the top of this file: so that the engineering can
   be reviewed and audited. Anyone who wants their statement removed can ask
   the copyright holder, and it will be withdrawn.

   Names of individual posters are not recorded. Where a practitioner's
   nickname had been captured incidentally in an internal note, it was removed
   on 2026-09-02; the surrounding statement and its source URL remain, because
   a claim whose source cannot be checked is worse than no claim.


4. NO WARRANTY

   The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied. The copyright holder is not liable for any claim, damage or other
   liability arising from this software or its use.


5. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

   This repository refers to and interoperates with third-party models, weights
   and packages that carry their own licences. Those licences are not granted or
   modified by this file and remain the responsibility of whoever runs the code.
   Note in particular that the identity instrument uses InsightFace buffalo_l
   weights, which are licensed for non-commercial use only: the acceptance
   layer as shipped is a development instrument, not a resellable component.


6. HOW TO OBTAIN RIGHTS

   Permission to use any part of this work is available by agreement. Ask.


